Random 'some class of monster' is subject to A dlvl/XL dependent 
monster generation process, however it is different then the normal 
random monster generation. The process is capable of generating out of 
depth monsters, but it will be rare.

Assuming I'm reading mkclass() correctly this is roughly how it works:
The game generates a 'maximum monster level' of dlvl/2
The game find the last valid monster of a class (assumes that all 
monsters of a class are grouped together in order of increasing 
strength, stops at first invalid monster). All monsters are valid if 
they are less then the 'maximum monster level'. If greater then the 
'maximum monster level' then will be valid 50% of the time.
The game then picks a monster of the class requested that appears 
before the last valid monster. The pick is weighted by generation 
frequency, and also by players xlvl (weaker players will tend to have 
weaker monsters).



